# UI and motion

## Lenis (`@repo/ui`)

`SmoothScrollProvider` drives Lenis via `motion-dom`'s shared rAF — do not enable Lenis `autoRaf`.

```ts
// packages/ui/src/smooth-scroll-provider.tsx pattern
options={{ autoRaf: false, lerp: 0.125, anchors: true, autoToggle: true }}
frame.update(update, true) // sync with Motion
```

- `LenisRouteSync` calls `lenis.resize()` on pathname change.
- Mount `SmoothScrollProvider` once in root layout — not per-page.

## Motion

Import from `motion/react` (not `framer-motion`).

```ts
import { motion, useScroll, useTransform } from 'motion/react'
```

`useScroll` + `useTransform` pair with Lenis because both share the `motion-dom` frame. See `parallax-section.tsx` for the reference pattern.

Keep `motion-dom` version aligned with `motion` — both are pinned in `@repo/ui`.

## Reduced motion

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`:
- Hide or skip decorative animations (see `intro.css` pattern).
- Do not force scroll smoothing or parallax when reduced motion is preferred.
- Provide skip controls for long entrance animations.

## CSS-only animation

Prefer CSS keyframes from `src/styles/tokens/motion.css` for simple transitions. Reserve Motion for scroll-linked transforms.

## Client boundary

All Motion and Lenis components require `'use client'`. Keep animation logic in `components/effects/` or `@repo/ui`.
